  "description": "These subtle signals helped me identify the 2020 and 2022 bottom",
  "body_html": "<p>We have been talking about a stock market collapse for over 2 years; a market melt-down. A melt down comes<em><strong> after</strong></em> a <a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/melt-up.asp\">stock market melt up</a>…rapidly rising asset prices with low volume in poor economic conditions. Now whether we have officially entered-into the melt down…or there is still a blow off top to be seen… we will not know until in hindsight. However, there are a few things we can confirm.</p><ul><li><p>The power of hindsight allows us to confirm, the melt up did occur.</p></li><li><p>Only 1 of 2 events can come after a melt up:</p><ul><li><p>Blow off top: A massive retail liquidity trap</p></li><li><p>A melt down…whether now or after the blow off top.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p>Let me be crystal clear, as I have tried to do in my video posts as well: <strong>EVEN IF A BLOW OFF TOP WERE TO HAPPEN, IT IS A TRAP AND IS NOT SOMETHING TO INVEST INTO.</strong> Sorry, it is unbelievable how many watch10 seconds of a video and skip the most important parts. Regardless…a blow off top could still happen; however the probabilities look lower as of late. I am not trying to time a potential blow off top and am ~98% cash right now. And will remain so, aside from smaller short term trades, when and if they appear. </p><p>Whatever  happens to the stock market in the short term, <em><strong>this piece is written for the long-term investors who are seeking “when” to buy back in</strong></em>. We do not “buy the dip” or “dollar cost average”.</p><p>There are no magical chart indicators…nor are we trying to time a bottom…<strong>here are 6 major clues the bottom is in…</strong></p>",
  "has_dynamic_content": false,
  "truncated_body_text": "We have been talking about a stock market collapse for over 2 years; a market melt-down. A melt down comes after a stock market melt up…rapidly rising asset prices with low volume in poor economic conditions. Now whether we have officially entered-into the melt down…or there is still a blow off top to be seen… we will not know until in hindsight. However, there are a few things we can confirm.",
